  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 4603.01 Written Estimate of Costs",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 4603.01 Written Estimate of Costs.\n\n(a) Upon the request of any shipper, a household goods carrier shall provide a written estimate of costs in advance of performing any service for the shipper.\n\n(b) A written estimate of costs shall contain the following:\n\n(1) For shipments transported at hourly rates:\n\na. The name and address of the carrier to perform the services;\n\nb. The name and title of the person preparing the estimate;\n\nc. The origin and destination of the proposed transport and the mileage between such points;\n\nd. The rate to be applied;\n\ne. An itemized statement of all accessorial services to be performed and the applicable charges; and\n\nf. An estimate of the total of all charges;\n\n(2) For shipments transported on weight and mileage rates:\n\na. The information required (1)a.- f. above;\n\nb. A list of the articles upon which the estimate is based and the applicable estimated cubic footage for each article listed; and\n\nc. The estimated total weight of the shipment, based upon a conversion formula of no less than 7 pounds per cubic foot; and\n\n(3) A statement that the carrier shall not charge the customer any amount which exceeds the written estimate by 10 percent without the customer’s written consent.\n\nSource. #13828, eff 12-22-23 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 4600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c4600.html"
}
